{"kind":"propose","text":"H2 starts from published 95ec0456, which contains H1 via 1f81ac01. The effective sequence and prepare-clock slice can proceed independently. I propose a pure derive reservation interface for the other slice: before the member requests a position, compare its current use and owed work plus a conservative five-dimension envelope for the selected input. After judgment, compare the actual prepare draft plus one settlement and downstream work derived from its effects. Reserve one outcome for the order scope’s own allocation. Keep prepare’s reserved work separate from live indexes until commit transfers it or abandon releases it. H4 owns persistence and the fence. The current fits takes only scopeEntries and reserved sees only the input tag, so a tag cannot recover the prepared downstream terms. Is the preflight envelope an explicit bounded term the future H4 caller supplies, or should H2 derive it today from the selected definition branch, and which retained-byte terms must it carry? H1’s SequencedInput already admits a wrapped act or request delivery while version 1 marks acts only. I propose exercising both admitted wrapper forms in the pure fold, without widening v1 admission. I also propose distinguishing verified prepare sources inside derive’s delivery judgment now, while leaving the Scope delivery response transition for H4 and keeping creation acceptance bounded to its existing reasons. Please rule on this boundary or point to the existing ruling."}